      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many hospitals cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. At this dose there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours**, or four times daily with a 4,000 mg/day cap if your institution allows it\n- **3000 mg total daily**, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me which regimen you want, or confirm that 3000 mg three times daily is intended, and I'll enter it. For a 70 kg adult with normal liver function and no allergies, the first option is a common choice."
      }
     ],
