     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 9,000 mg/day is a toxic dose, and no indication I know of supports it. Each 3,000 mg dose alone is in the range where hepatotoxicity becomes a concern, and three of them in a day would likely cause serious liver injury. Normal baseline liver function doesn't change that.\n\nIf the order is intentional, for example because of an unusual protocol, it needs a pharmacist or attending to review and enter it through your institution's override process. I can't do that on my own.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf the goal is stronger pain control or fever control, I can also help with adding a different drug to the regimen. Which would you like?"
      }
